  "question": "How does Intel's treatment of shares withheld for taxes on RSUs differ from Apple's settlement process?",
  "answer": "Intel treats withheld shares as repurchases, while Apple deducts them from the total shares delivered to the participant.",
  "quote_a": "less any Shares that may be withheld to satisfy the Tax-Related Items",
  "quote_b": "we treat shares of common stock withheld for tax purposes on behalf of our employees in connection with the vesting of RSUs as common stock repurchases"
}
